Original commit body from 3047d6d:

Call edges now point to function definitions (.c, .cpp files) instead of
declarations (.h files). This fixes transitive test coverage estimation
for C/C++ codebases where the previous behavior could truncate the call
graph at header file declarations (which have no outgoing call edges).

The fix processes header files before source files during file discovery,
so that definitions naturally replace declarations when building the
global symbol registry. This ensures call edge resolution uses the
definition (with its outgoing call edges) rather than the declaration.

Discovered while investigating why quadlet repo showed only 7% estimated
coverage - the actual issue was that call edges were pointing to header
declarations that had no bodies and therefore no outgoing calls.
